# Protections for the untrusted-library-search-path corpus (CWE-426 / CWE-427).
#
# The five PROTECTION lines at the bottom of this file are IDENTICAL -- byte for
# byte -- in every target of this family, including the negative control, so a
# per-target difference in outcome can never be attributed to different hardening.
# The only lines that differ between targets are the LINKER lines that express
# that target's loader-influence mechanism (-ldl, -Wl,-rpath,..., the DT_NEEDED
# sibling), and each of those is documented in the target's own section below.
#
# EVERY PROTECTION IS ON, AND NONE OF THEM MATTERS. That is the point of the
# category, not an oversight. This is a filesystem + dynamic-loader category and
# it is orthogonal to the entire memory-safety mitigation stack:
#
# -fstack-protector-all  a canary detects a corrupted return address in an
#                        epilogue. Nothing here writes past a buffer; no frame is
#                        ever damaged, so the check always passes. The "payload"
#                        is an ELF shared object sitting in a directory.
# -pie -fPIE             PIE randomises where code and data live. No step of this
#                        exploit needs any address at all: the attacker never
#                        computes a pointer, and the code that runs is code the
#                        LOADER mapped and relocated on the attacker's behalf.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    Full RELRO write-protects the GOT after startup. There is
#                        no GOT write here and no pointer write of any kind. Worth
#                        noting the opposite effect on libhj_13: -z now means every
#                        relocation is resolved BEFORE any constructor runs, so a
#                        planted DT_NEEDED object that fails to define the init
#                        symbol aborts the process instead of running -- the
#                        mitigation constrains the exploit's SHAPE without
#                        preventing it.
# (NX)                   comes from the default program headers. Nothing is
#                        executed from a data page: the attacker's code is in the
#                        .text of a legitimately mapped, legitimately executable
#                        shared object.
#
# -O0                    load-bearing for the MEASUREMENT, not for the bug. The
#                        executor derives the mechanism by reading call sites and
#                        their rodata string arguments out of the image (which
#                        dlopen argument is relative, which is a bare soname,
#                        which getenv value reaches the path builder), and at
#                        higher -O those arguments can live only in registers
#                        across inlined code. The bug is a loader-configuration
#                        defect and is entirely unaffected by optimisation level.
#
# THIS TARGET'S MECHANISM LINE: none. The loader influence is the
# opendir/readdir/dlopen scan in the source. NO DT_RUNPATH and NO DT_RPATH.
-ldl
#
# --- protections, identical across the family -----------------------------
-fstack-protector-all
-pie
-fPIE
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
